A sum of Rs. 550 was taken as a loan to be paid back in two equal installments. If the rate of interest is 20% per annum compounded annually, the value of each installment is
Rs. 220
Rs. 300
Rs. 360
Rs. 720
Solution:
Formula: The present value of the two installments must equal the loan.
Let each installment be Rs. x, paid at the end of year 1 and year 2.
x / (1 + 20/100) + x / (1 + 20/100)² = 550
x/1.2 + x/1.44 = 550
x × (1.2 + 1) / 1.44 = 550
x × 2.2 / 1.44 = 550
x = 550 × 1.44 / 2.2 = Rs. 360
Check:
Year 1: 550 × 1.2 = 660. After paying 360, the balance is 300.
Year 2: 300 × 1.2 = 360. After paying 360, the balance is 0 ✓

The correct option is Rs. 360.
